# Copper effects, proven pixel by pixel. Column x=8 below the HUD has no walls
# or sprite, so it shows COLOR00 exactly as the copper set it on each line.
# Expected colours come from logic.c (logicLineColor with logicBarY(frame));
# 'early' shows bar frame 13 (bar top y=49), 'late' frame 105 (bar top y=198).
wait 10
screenshot early

# (a) Sky gradient: COLOR00 differs from band to band (a 2-bitplane screen,
# 58 background colours).
expect-color early 8 28 0x001
expect-color early 8 100 0x44B
expect-color early 8 150 0xB59
expect-color early 8 210 0xFA5
expect-color early 8 212 0xFA6
expect-color early 8 255 0xFFB

# (b) Palette split at y=24: the same registers, different colours.
# COLOR00: HUD black above, sky below.
expect-color early 200 10 0x000
expect-color early 200 28 0x001
# COLOR01 (box fill): HUD gold vs wall blue.
expect-color early 12 10 0xFC0
expect-color early 70 100 0x468
# COLOR02 (box edge, HUD rule): HUD brown vs wall edge.
expect-color early 8 10 0xA50
expect-color early 200 23 0xA50
expect-color early 64 100 0x9BD

# (c) The raster bar moves: at 'early' it covers y=49..64.
expect-color early 8 49 0x013
expect-color early 8 56 0xEFF
expect-color early 8 205 0xF95

wait 92
screenshot late
# ...92 frames later it covers y=198..213: y=56 is sky again, y=205 is bar.
expect-color late 8 56 0x125
expect-color late 8 205 0xEFF
# The bar crosses beam line 255 (y=211) -> 256 (y=212): one colour per line,
# no line late or missing around the WAIT wrap.
expect-color late 8 210 0x079
expect-color late 8 211 0x057
expect-color late 8 212 0x035
expect-color late 8 213 0x013
expect-color late 8 214 0xFA6
# The bar is COLOR00, so it passes behind the walls: wall pixels unchanged.
expect-color late 150 205 0x468
# The HUD palette is restored at the top of every frame.
expect-color late 12 10 0xFC0
expect-color late 200 10 0x000
expect-no-serial "ERR|STACK SMASHED"
